            "type": "text",
            "category": "Other",
            "value": "Disposition: suspicious (confidence: medium); run 2026-07-31T09:14:22Z/7f31.\nPeriod examined: 2026-07-17 00:00:00+00:00 → 2026-07-31 09:00:00+00:00.\n[enumerate-spn-requests] suspicious: Three service accounts show RC4-only TGS bursts sourced from the workstation VLAN rather than the admin VLAN.\n[check-volume] suspicious: Request volume exceeded the threshold, so triage proceeded.\n[triage] suspicious: The burst pattern and non-admin source subnets are consistent with kerberoasting, but no credential-rotation change record was found that would explain the activity benignly. Host process ancestry could not be checked, so an approved scanner remains possible.\nSupports malicious: RC4-only TGS requests for accounts that normally negotiate AES; request sources outside the administrative VLAN\nUnknown: whether an approved vulnerability scanner ran in the window; whether a credential-rotation job touched these accounts\nNot examined — edr: Process ancestry for the requesting hosts was not examined, so an approved scanner could not be ruled out as the source.",
